  "decision_reasons": [
    "Main-seed aggregate throughput increases 3.79%, but the second seed falls 4.78% and its p95 rises from1814 to1951ms. Only7/20 second-seed pairs favor the candidate.",
    "The custom-bound control has zero prepared columns yet improves6.92%, larger than the active main-seed change. This limits causal attribution rather than excusing the second-seed regression.",
    "Instrumented mushroom replay falls to about3ms, but preparation absorbs nearly all of the prior interval. Including both phases, brown mushrooms measure63.21ms versus58.74ms in the earlier main-seed observer and45.85ms versus45.33ms for seed42. These are separate instrumented observations, not matched ordinary timing.",
    "Counter controls retain exactly the same anchor, column and prefix builds for every case. Main prepares7814 columns; seed42 prepares7906. Seed42 generates8627 terrain chunks versus8529, showing scheduling can change bounded-cache work. Worker wait counters overlap and must not be interpreted as wall-time fractions.",
    "Output parity and unit proof establish validity of the narrow preparation transformation, not a useful speedup. No additional concurrent/lifecycle acceptance is selected for this held prototype."
  ],
  "next_investigation": "Examine a bounded job-owned queue for exact prerequisite anchors with cooperative waits restricted to strictly earlier dependency levels. This would let waiting workers help the blocked owner without arbitrary Rayon steals, duplicate initialization or feature replay. Audit dependency levels, single-owner/error/panic handling, lost wakeups, ownership at root completion and slot-size cost before implementing. The design is a hypothesis, not a measured benefit; see external dependency-scheduling-hypothesis.md.",
  "limitations": [
    "Quiet timing, no-regression and subsecond confirmation remain deferred by user.",
    "Only the two standard profiles contain eligible active roots; custom profiles and Overworld are controls for this transformation.",
    "Observer occupancy covers subsequent anchor evaluation only. Preparation is a separate recorded phase and stays within complete-region timing.",
    "A one-warmup/one-measured-region diagnostic provides workload counts only; it is not a latency acceptance run.",
    "Paired process peaks include engine startup/warmups and two resident isolated processes, exclude later NBT comparisons, and do not prove a sustained memory bound.",
    "No production scheduler change is selected by these observations. C61 remains isolated from accepted main."
  ],
